      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has one monolithic test method testing two distinct behaviors (merge mode vs. non-merge/replace mode), plus edge cases. I'll improve understandability by:\n- Splitting into focused test methods with descriptive names\n- Using clearer variable names\n- Removing the unused `_set` helper\n- Adding assertion messages for clarityNow I'll compile-check the file.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file splits the original single monolithic test into three focused, self-documenting test methods — one for merge-mode (union behaviour), one for non-merge mode (replace behaviour), and one for the null/empty override edge cases — with descriptive assertion messages throughout."
